hat the thread is working correctly.\n',1,'s25'),('b2lovegr',2,4,'2025-06-26_17-41-28','The code would crash without using the set PSP function as if PSP isn’t set then the thread wouldn’t have a set place to start so it would start wherever it last was and execute code that doesn’t make sense so then it would crash.\n',0,'s25'),('b2lovegr',2,4,'2025-06-26_19-01-32','The code would crash without using the set PSP function as if PSP isn’t set then the thread wouldn’t have a set place to start so it would start wherever it last was and execute code that doesn’t make sense so then it would crash.\n',0,'s25'),('b2lovegr',2,4,'2025-06-27_10-08-53','The code would crash without using the set PSP function as if PSP isn’t set to the specific start of the thread stack which differs from the MSP stack which is used by the kernel, then the thread wouldn’t know where to start. It would start at the last value of the pointer, which the programmer can’t really control and execute code that is likely invalid so then it would crash. The __set_PSP function allows for the location to be set to the start of the stack so that it can pop the appropriate values and then execute the thread in the correct order.\n',1,'s25'),('b2lovegr',2,4,'2025-06-27_12-22-31','The code would crash without using the set PSP function as if PSP isn’t set to the specific start of the thread stack which differs from the MSP stack which is used by the kernel, then the thread wouldn’t know where to start. It would start at the last value of the pointer, which the programmer can’t really control and execute code that is likely invalid so then it would crash. The __set_PSP function allows for the location to be set to the start of the stack so that it can pop the appropriate values and then execute the thread in the correct order.\n',1,'s25'),('b2lovegr',2,4,'2025-06-27_13-21-27','The code would crash without using the set PSP function as if PSP isn’t set to the specific start of the thread stack which differs fr