priate values and then execute the thread in the correct order.\n',1,'s25'),('b2lovegr',2,4,'2025-06-27_19-46-42','The code would crash without using the set PSP function as if PSP isn’t set to the specific start of the thread stack which differs from the MSP stack which is used by the kernel, then the thread wouldn’t know where to start. It would start at the last value of the pointer, which the programmer can’t really control and execute code that is likely invalid so then it would crash. The __set_PSP function allows for the location to be set to the start of the stack so that it can pop the appropriate values and then execute the thread in the correct order.\n',1,'s25'),('b2lovegr',2,4,'2025-06-27_20-01-39','The code would crash without using the set PSP function as if PSP isn’t set to the specific start of the thread stack which differs from the MSP stack which is used by the kernel, then the thread wouldn’t know where to start. It would start at the last value of the pointer, which the programmer can’t really control and execute code that is likely invalid so then it would crash. The __set_PSP function allows for the location to be set to the start of the stack so that it can pop the appropriate values and then execute the thread in the correct order.\n',1,'s25'),('b2lovegr',2,5,'2025-06-26_17-41-28','If the thread simply printed something once and then returned then after it returned the thread should be terminated. To do that we would need to deallocate any of the resources that were assigned to the thread.\n',0,'s25'),('b2lovegr',2,5,'2025-06-26_19-01-32','If the thread simply printed something once and then returned then after it returned the thread should be terminated. To do that we would need to deallocate any of the resources that were assigned to the thread.\n',0,'s25'),('b2lovegr',2,5,'2025-06-27_10-08-53','If the thread simply printed something once and then returned it would be missing a return address. If the address is missing the thread would not know where to go in memory once the thread has been completed. Since the thread doesn’t know where to execute it would likely hard fault.\n',0,'s25'),('b2lovegr',2,5,'2025-06-27_12-22-31','If the thread simply printed something once and then returned it would be missing a return address as this isn’t defined in the thread. If the address is missing the Cortex M4 would not know where to go in memory once the thread has been completed. Since the thread doesn’t know where to execute it would likely hard fault. This can be prevented by having a return address that can be popped and that contains the location of the instructions that the OS needs to run next.\n',0,'s25'),('b2lovegr',2,5,'2025-06-27_13-21-27','If the thread simply printed something once and then returned it would be missing a return address as this isn’t defined in the thread. If the address is missing the Cortex M4 would not know where to go in memory once the thread has been completed. Since the thread doesn’t know where to execute it would likely execute at an invalid address which would cause the thread to hard fault. This can be prevented by having a return address that can be popped and that contains the location of the instructions that the OS needs to run next.\n',0,'s25'),('b2lovegr',2,5,'2025-06-27_14-29-51','If the thread simply printed something once and then returned it would be missing a return address as this isn’t defined in the thread. If the address is missing the Cortex M4 would not know where to go in memory once the thread has been completed and it would likely go to an invalid address which would cause the thread to hard fault. This can be prevented by having a return address that can be popped that contains the location of the instructions that the OS needs to run next.\n',1,'s25'),('b2lovegr',2,5,'2025-06-27_15-12-27','If the thread simply printed something once and then returned it would be missing a return address as this isn’t defined in the thread. If the address is missing t