nd passes the function they would like to run. The function to create the thread then allocates the appropriate memory and returns whether it was successfully created.\nIf the thread returns successfully then the user can call the thread to run, if it returns false then the user would not be able to run the thread.\n',0,'s25'),('b2lovegr',3,3,'2025-06-27_12-47-15','From the user’s perspective you first need to initialize the kernel.\nNext the user needs to have defined a function the user wants to run in the thread itself. This can be any function the user wants but they need to have defined it somewhere.\nNext the user then calls the create thread function and passes the function they would like to run. The function to create the thread then allocates the appropriate memory and returns whether it was successfully created.\nIf the thread returns successfully then the user can call the thread to run by starting the kernel which launches the first thread, if it returns false then the user would not be able to run the thread.\n',0,'s25'),('b2lovegr',3,3,'2025-06-27_13-35-33','From the user’s perspective you first need to initialize the kernel. This sets up the initial data needed for the thread to set up.\nNext the user needs to write a function that they want the thread to run. This can be any function the user wants but they need to have defined it somewhere.\nNext the user then calls the create thread function and passes the function they would like to run. Then the create thread function initializes the value and places the thread in the kernel thread list.\nIf the thread returns successfully then the user can call the thread to run by starting the kernel which launches the first thread, if it returns false then the user would not be able to run the thread.\n',1,'s25'),('b2lovegr',3,3,'2025-06-27_14-18-53','From the user’s perspective you first need to initialize the kernel. This sets up the initial data needed for the thread to set up.\nNext the user needs to writ