'),('b2lovegr',4,1,'2025-07-30_15-04-22','A queue is interesting because it isn’t an array. The queue has a benefit as it takes up less space as everything will be stored beside each other in memory. The thread will dequeue from the front of the queue and run that thread then after it has finished running it would queue it at the back of the queue and repeat the process. This allows for more efficient use as if a thread ever needs to be removed you don’t need to move things around in the array and everything will get equal treatment.\n',0,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,1,'2025-07-30_15-40-21','A queue is interesting because it isn’t an array. The queue has a benefit as it takes up less space as everything will be stored beside each other in memory. The thread will dequeue from the front of the queue and run that thread then after it has finished running it would queue it at the back of the queue and repeat the process. This allows for more efficient use as if a thread ever needs to be removed you don’t need to move things around in the array and everything will get equal treatment. This is different from the current array based scheduler as it is taking a modulus the placement of the threads has to be correct in the array or else it won’t load properly (i.e. if the thread isn’t present in index 0).\n',0,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,1,'2025-07-30_19-59-05','A queue is interesting because it isn’t an array. The queue has a benefit as it takes up less space as everything will be stored beside each other in memory. The thread will dequeue from the front of the queue and run that thread then after it has finished running it would queue it at the back of the queue and repeat the process. This allows for more efficient use as if a thread ever needs to be removed you don’t need to move things around in the array and everything will get equal treatment. This is different from the current array-based scheduler as it is taking a modulus the placement of the threads has to be correct in the array or else it won’t load properly (i.e. if the thread isn’t present in index 0). While this is similar as it cycles through the different threads one at a time in order it does require more computing to make it work if a thread is removed from the array.\n',0,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,1,'2025-07-30_21-53-00','A queue is interesting because it isn’t an array. The queue has a benefit as it takes up less space as everything will be stored beside each other in memory. The thread will dequeue from the front of the queue and run that thread then after it has finished running it would queue it at the back of the queue and repeat the process. This allows for more efficient use as if a thread ever needs to be removed you don’t need to move things around in the array and everything will get equal treatment. This is different from the current array-based scheduler as it is taking a modulus the placement of the threads has to be correct in the array or else it won’t load properly (i.e. if the thread isn’t present in index 0). However this acts much like a queue.\n',1,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,1,'2025-07-30_22-39-57','A queue is interesting because it isn’t an array. The queue has a benefit as it takes up less space as everything will be stored beside each other in memory. The thread will dequeue from the front of the queue and run that thread then after it has finished running it would queue it at the back of the queue and repeat the process. This allows for more efficient use as if a thread ever needs to be removed you don’t need to move things around in the array and everything will get equal treatment. This is different from the current array-based scheduler as it is taking a modulus the placement of the threads has to be correct in the array or else it won’t load properly (i.e. if the thread isn’t present in index 0). However this acts much like a queue.\n',1,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,1,'2025-07-30_23-05-02','A queue is interesting because it isn’t an array. The queue has a benefit as it takes up less space as everything will be stored beside each other in memory. The thread will dequeue from the front of the queue and run that thread then after it has finished running it would queue it at the back of the queue and repeat the process. This allows for more efficient use as if a thread ever needs to be removed you don’t need to move things around in the array and everything will get equal treatment. This is different from the current array-based scheduler as it is taking a modulus the placement of the threads has to be correct in the array or else it won’t load properly (i.e. if the thread isn’t present in index 0). However this acts much like a queue.\n',1,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,2,'2025-07-30_14-14-04','The PendSV_Handler preforms a context switch by storing the stack pointer in the thread’s structure. It then changes the current thread to the next thread and then finally changes PSP to the current threads stack pointer\n',0,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,2,'2025-07-30_14-45-39','The PendSV_Handler preforms a context switch by storing the stack pointer located in PSP in the thread’s structure. It then has to copy over R0-4 into storage and then it uses osSched to decide which thread to switch. It then changes the current thread to the next thread and then finally changes PSP to the current threads stack pointer\n',0,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,2,'2025-07-30_15-04-22','The PendSV_Handler preforms a context switch by storing the stack pointer located in PSP in the thread’s structure. It then has to copy over R4-11 into storage and then it uses osSched to decide which thread to switch. It then changes the current thread to the next thread and then finally changes PSP to the current threads stack pointer\n',0,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,2,'2025-07-30_15-40-21','The PendSV_Handler preforms a context switch by storing the stack pointer located in PSP in the thread’s structure. It then has to copy over R4-11 into memory and then it uses osSched to decide which thread to switch to. It then changes the current thread to the next thread and then finally changes PSP to the current threads stack pointer. Then after the registers R4-11 are filled again from memory execution can resume.\n',0,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,2,'2025-07-30_19-59-05','The PendSV_Handler preforms a context switch by storing the stack pointer located in PSP in the thread’s structure. It then has to copy over R4-11 into memory and then it uses osSched to decide which thread to switch to. It then changes the current thread to the next thread and then finally changes PSP to the current threads stack pointer. Then after the registers R4-11 are filled again to the new thread’s stack from memory execution can resume.\n',0,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,2,'2025-07-30_21-53-00','The PendSV_Handler preforms a context switch by storing the stack pointer located in PSP in the thread’s structure. It then has to copy over R4-11 into the stack and then it uses osSched to decide which thread to switch to. It then changes the current thread to the next thread and then finally changes PSP to the current threads stack pointer. Then after the registers R4-11 are filled again by popping off the stack, execution can resume.\n',0,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,2,'2025-07-30_22-39-57','The PendSV_Handler preforms a context switch by storing the stack pointer located in PSP in the thread’s structure. It then has to push R4-11 into the stack and then it uses osSched to decide which thread to switch to. It then changes the PSP to the new threads stack pointer. Then after the registers R4-11 are filled again by popping off the stack, execution for the new stack can begin.\n',1,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,2,'2025-07-30_23-05-02','The PendSV_Handler preforms a context switch by storing the stack pointer located in PSP in the thread’s structure. It then has to push R4-11 into the stack and then it uses osSched to decide which thread to switch to. It then changes the PSP to the new threads stack pointer. Then after the registers R4-11 are filled again by popping off the stack, execution for the new stack can begin.\n',1,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,3,'2025-07-30_14-14-04','This is a bad idea as any thread that has a lower priority will never be ran. This creates issues as there are other threads that will need to be run and this is why a system like round robin works better.\n',1,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,3,'2025-07-30_14-45-39','This is a bad idea as any thread that has a lower priority will never be ran. This creates issues as there are other threads that will need to be run and this is why a system like round robin works better.\n',1,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,3,'2025-07-30_15-04-22','This is a bad idea as any thread that has a lower priority will never be ran. This creates issues as there are other threads that will need to be run and this is why a system like round robin works better.\n',1,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,3,'2025-07-30_15-40-21','This is a bad idea as any thread that has a lower priority will never be ran. This creates issues as there are other threads that will need to be run and this is why a system like round robin works better.\n',1,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,3,'2025-07-30_19-59-05','This is a bad idea as any thread that has a lower priority will never be ran. This creates issues as there are other threads that will need to be run and this is why a system like round robin works better.\n',1,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,3,'2025-07-30_21-53-00','This is a bad idea as any thread that has a lower priority will never be ran. This creates issues as there are other threads that will need to be run and this is why a system like round robin works better.\n',1,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,3,'2025-07-30_22-39-57','This is a bad idea as any thread that has a lower priority will never be ran. This creates issues as there are other threads that will need to be run and this is why a system like round robin works better.\n',1,'s25'),('b2lovegr',4,3,'2025-07-30_23-05-02','This is a bad idea as any thread that has a lower priority will never be r