ccess to these resources. The system call allows the program to contact the OS through the kernel to request a service that it cannot perform. The OS then performs the operations required and returns to the program.\n',1,'s25'),('kbsavla',2,2,'2025-06-27_21-27-47','A system call is a function call from the user program requesting to the OS that it needs to perform a task the program cannot do due to the OS having restrictions on resource access and memory to protect the hardware from unknown code. As a result, the system call must be used to gain access to these resources. The system call allows the program to contact the OS through the kernel to request a service that it cannot perform. The OS then performs the operations required and returns to the program.\n',1,'s25'),('kbsavla',2,3,'2025-05-27_10-42-39','The stack was set up by first navigating to the memory address of the PSP, which becomes the start of the stack for the thread. The pointer to the stack must be declared and set to the address obtained. Next, the register values need to be pushed onto the thread’s stack. This shows us what it means “to set up a thread’s stack.” It means to load all the required registers to run the thread. These values need to be on the stack so the CPU knows what instructions to execute.\n',0,'s25'),('kbsavla',2,3,'2025-05-27_13-20-12','The stack was set up by first navigating to the memory address of the PSP, which becomes the start of the stack for the thread. The pointer to the stack must be declared and set to the address obtained. The stack is then allocated from that value in the memory. Next, the register values need to be pushed onto the thread’s stack. This shows us what it means to set up a thread’s stack.” It means to load all the required registers to run the thread. These values need to be on the stack so the CPU knows what instructions to execute. This is because the CPU simply runs programs; it does not assign values. Therefore, if there is a new thread with a new stack,  the CPU will not have any instructions to run it. Thus, when running the new thread, it is as if it were running before, and the CPU is just restoring the state. To restore the state, it must have values to restore. Additionally, the value restoration order must be correct to ensure that the CPU assign the correct values to the correct registers.\n',1,'s25'),('kbsavla',2,3,'2025-06-26_00-32-12','The stack was set up by first navigating to the memory address of the PSP, which becomes the start of the stack for the thread. The pointer to the stack must be declared and set to the address obtained. The stack is then allocated from that value in the memory. Next, the register values need to be pushed onto the thread’s stack. This shows us what it means to set up a thread’s stack.” It means to load all the required registers to run the thread. These values need to be on the stack so the CPU knows what instructions to execute. This is because the CPU simply runs programs; it does not assign values. Therefore, if there is a new thread with a new stack,  the CPU will not have any instructions to run it. Thus, when running the new thread, it is as if it were running before, and the CPU is just restoring the state. To restore the state, it must have values to restore. Additionally, the value restoration order must be correct to ensure that the CPU assign the correct values to the correct registers.\n',1,'s25'),('kbsavla',2,3,'2025-06-26_11-23-30','The stack was set up by first navigating to the memory address of the PSP, which becomes the start of the stack for the thread. The pointer to the stack must be declared and set to the address obtained. The stack is then allocated from that value in the memory. Next, the register values need to be pushed onto the thread’s stack. This shows us what it means to set up a thread’s stack.” It means to load all the required registers to run the thread. These values need to be on the stack so the CPU knows what instructions to exe